  <section slot="mid" class="bg-white py-16">
    <div class="container-slim max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-gold-700 mb-4">One Office, Every Age</p>
      <h2 class="display-2 mb-5">Dentistry for a household, not just a patient</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">
        The blocks between Douglas Manor and the Alley Pond edge of the neighborhood are full of long-tenure households — people who bought a house and stayed. What that means in a dental chair is that we're often seeing a seven-year-old's sealants in the morning and that child's grandparent for an implant restoration in the afternoon. Having general, cosmetic and restorative dentistry under one roof keeps those visits coordinated instead of scattered across three referrals.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong class="text-slate-700 font-semibold">Kids and teens:</strong> first exams, sealants, fluoride, mouthguards for school sports, and Invisalign when the timing is right.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-700 font-semibold">Adults:</strong> cleanings and gum care, whitening and veneers, crowns, root canals and nightguards for grinding.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-700 font-semibold">Older patients:</strong> implants, bridges, dentures and full-mouth work planned with 3D imaging before anything is started.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section slot="before-map" class="bg-sand-50 py-16 border-t border-brand-100/50">
    <div class="container-slim max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="display-2 mb-5">Built around the commute</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">
        Plenty of people here take the Port Washington Branch into Penn Station or Grand Central in the morning. Our Tuesday hours run to 7 PM so an appointment can sit on the end of a workday rather than the middle of one, and we're open 9 AM to 3 PM on both Saturday and Sunday. Because we're one stop from Douglaston station, coming straight off the train is realistic — no car, no parking, no detour.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
        We also hold same-day slots for emergencies. Broken tooth, lost filling, swelling that woke you up: call (718) 225-6677 and we'll get you seen rather than sending you to an urgent care that can only hand you antibiotics.
      </p>
    </div>
